1
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:30,000
The best in the business is back in the game.

2
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:54,000
Transporter 2 is a action, thriller, crime film directed by Louis Leterrier.

3
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:18,000
Professional driver, and former Special Forces officer, Frank Martin is living in Miami, where he is temporarily
filling in for a friend as the chauffeur for a government narcotics control policy director and his family.

4
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:42,000
The young boy in the family is targeted for kidnapping, and Frank immediately
becomes involved in protecting the child and exposing the kidnappers.

5
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:06,000
Frank Martin, played by Jason Statham.

6
00:26:24,000 --> 00:26:30,000
Audrey Billings, played by Amber Valletta.

7
00:30:48,000 --> 00:30:54,000
Gianni Chellini, played by Alessandro Gassmann.

8
00:35:12,000 --> 00:35:18,000
Lola, played by Kate Nauta.

9
00:39:36,000 --> 00:39:42,000
Jefferson Billings, played by Matthew Modine.

10
00:44:00,000 --> 00:44:06,000
Dimitri, played by Jason Flemyng.

11
00:48:24,000 --> 00:48:30,000
Transporter 2 (French: Le Transporteur 2) is a 2005 English-language French action film
directed by Louis Leterrier and written by Luc Besson & Robert Mark Kamen.

12
00:52:48,000 --> 00:52:54,000
It is the sequel to The Transporter (2002) and the second installment in the Transporter franchise,
followed by Transporter 3 (2008) and The Transporter Refueled, also called Transporter 4.

13
00:57:12,000 --> 00:57:18,000
It stars Jason Statham as Frank Martin, with Alessandro Gassmann, Amber Valletta,
Kate Nauta, François Berléand, Matthew Modine, and Jason Flemyng.

14
01:01:36,000 --> 01:01:42,000
In the film, Frank Martin (Statham) is tasked with protecting the young son of
politician Jefferson Billings (Modine) from an international drugs cartel.

15
01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:06,000
Transporter 2 was theatrically released in France on August 3, 2005, by EuropaCorp, and was
released in the United States on September 2, 2005, by 20th Century Fox.

16
01:10:24,000 --> 01:10:30,000
It received mixed reviews from critics with praise for Statham's performance,
action sequences and direction, but criticism for its screenwriting.

17
01:14:48,000 --> 01:14:54,000
It grossed $89.1 million worldwide and was followed
by the sequel Transporter 3 (2008).

18
01:19:12,000 --> 01:19:18,000
The film explores themes of martial arts, chauffeur,
miami, florida, workaholic, war on drugs.

19
01:23:36,000 --> 01:23:42,000
The tone is intense.
